      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I imagine in the SDK this might be a version of the Expression Menu, but it fires Udon events instead of setting Expression Parameters. The biggest problem I see with this is that it would mess up the muscle-memory of pretty much everyone -- that could potentially be mitigated with some advance warning, and by having a World Actions item there, even if it's inactive, all the time.\n\nHaving an extra options thing there like Avatars have that lets you respawn quickly would be nice, too.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-21T19:09:22.495Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "While there is a rich set of UI components for building in-world User Interfaces (the SurRoom is a great example), sometimes you might just want your world to have a few config options that's always on hand for the user to adjust, and you don't want to go through the immense effort that a full blown UI would require.\n\nSo it would be nice if there was a way to simplistically add a top-level \"World Expressions\" menu-list to the cd-shaped expressions menu, where the world could add entries and set up callbacks to the world which would react to those menu selections.",
